let __v_13270 = Value::from("3 to 4 hours on low. Butter the slow cooker pot and put in 60g pudding rice, 700ml whole milk, 100ml cream, 40g sugar and a strip of lemon peel or a bay leaf: the extra milk is there because nothing evaporates in a slow cooker. Stir once after an hour and then leave the lid on, because lifting it drops the heat. Take the lid off for the last 30 minutes if you want the top to catch, and loosen it with milk before it goes into bowls.");
frame.store("_RICE_PUDDING_SLOW", __v_13270.clone())?;
let __v_13271 = Value::from("About 25 minutes. Use a big bowl, because it swells and boils up, and put in 60g pudding rice, 600ml whole milk, 40g sugar and a strip of lemon peel. Microwave on high for 10 minutes, stir, then 8 minutes, stir, then 5 minutes at a time until the rice is soft. It carries on cooking as it stands, so stop while it is still a little loose, and finish it under the grill if you want a browned top.");
frame.store("_RICE_PUDDING_MICROWAVE", __v_13271.clone())?;
let __v_13272 = Value::from("20 minutes on high pressure with a 10 minute natural release: 60g pudding rice, 600ml whole milk, 40g sugar and a strip of lemon peel in a dish on a trivet over water. Do not fill the pot more than half way, because milk froths up through the valve. Loosen it with milk once the pressure is down, and grill the top if you want it browned.");
