let __v_13320 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"parmesan\",\"parmesan cheese\",\"grana padano\",\"pecorino\",\"pecorino romano\"]},\"Probably not: Parmesan, Grana Padano and Pecorino are set with animal rennet, which comes from the stomach of a calf or a lamb, so the traditional ones are not vegetarian. Some supermarket versions use microbial rennet instead - the ingredient list or the Vegetarian Society logo is the only way to tell.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gelatin\",\"gelatine\",\"jelly\",\"jelly cubes\",\"marshmallow\",\"marshmallows\",\"haribo\",\"gummy sweets\",\"gummy bears\",\"gummies\",\"wine gums\",\"jelly babies\",\"chewy sweets\"]},\"Not if the packet says gelatin or gelatine: that is made from pork or beef skin and bone, so jelly, marshmallows, jelly babies and most gummy sweets are out. The vegetarian versions set with pectin, agar or carrageenan instead, and they say so on the front.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"worcestershire sauce\",\"worcester sauce\",\"worcestershire\"]},\"Not the ordinary Lea & Perrins: Worcestershire sauce is made with anchovies, so it is neither vegetarian nor vegan. Anchovy-free versions exist, and a splash of soy sauce or balsamic does the same job in a stew or a cheese on toast.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"caesar dressing\",\"caesar salad\",\"caesar\"]},\"No, not a classic one: Caesar dressing has anchovies and Parmesan, so the dressing and the salad with it are not vegetarian. Vegetarian versions swap the anchovy for capers and use a hard cheese made with microbial rennet.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pesto\",\"green pesto\",\"pesto sauce\"]},\"Usually not: jarred pesto is made with Parmesan or Pecorino, and both are set with animal rennet. Look for one labelled vegetarian, or make it with a vegetarian hard cheese - the basil, pine nuts, garlic and oil are all fine.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chips\",\"fries\",\"chip shop chips\",\"french fries\"]},\"Usually yes - potatoes and oil - but chip-shop chips can be fried in beef dripping, which is traditional in the north, and a shop that fries them in the same oil as the fish is a no for some people. Ask, or use oven chips and read the packet.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"croissant\",\"croissants\",\"pastry\",\"pastries\",\"danish\",\"pain au chocolat\",\"puff pastry\",\"shortcrust\"]},\"Yes: a croissant is flour, butter, yeast, sugar and egg, all of which are vegetarian, though not vegan. Ordinary pastry is vegetarian too, with one exception - some savoury pie pastry still lists lard, so read the packet before you assume.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stock cube\",\"stock cubes\",\"stock\",\"gravy\",\"gravy granules\",\"bouillon\"]},\"Read the packet: plenty of chicken and beef stock cubes are actually vegetarian, and plenty of 'vegetable' gravies have meat fat in them. The vegetarian ones are labelled, and a vegetable stock cube with a dash of soy sauce covers the same ground.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"feta\",\"feta cheese\"]},\"Usually yes: most supermarket feta is made with microbial rennet and says so on the back, while the traditional barrel-aged Greek and Bulgarian sorts use animal rennet, so read the label before you count on it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"halloumi\",\"halloumi cheese\"]},\"Often not: most halloumi is made with animal rennet, so look for vegetarian on the packet or the Vegetarian Society logo. The vegetarian versions grill and squeak the same way.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cheese\",\"cheddar\",\"mozzarella\",\"brie\",\"cottage cheese\",\"cream cheese\"]},\"Most cheese is fine, but the hard ones - Parmesan, Grana Padano, Pecorino, and some traditional cheddars - are set with animal rennet. Cheddar, mozzarella and cottage cheese are usually made with microbial rennet, and the Vegetarian Society logo settles it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"wine\",\"beer\",\"cider\",\"ale\",\"lager\",\"stout\"]},\"It may not be, technically: wine and beer are often fined with isinglass from fish swim bladders, gelatin or egg white, and the fining agent never appears on the label. Most supermarket bottles now print 'suitable for vegetarians', so buy one that does.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rice\",\"pasta\",\"bread\",\"noodles\",\"flour\",\"potatoes\"]},\"Yes: rice, pasta, noodles, flour and potatoes are vegetarian, and bread almost always is - the exception is lard in some traditional loaves. Egg pasta is still vegetarian, it is only vegan that rules it out.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chocolate\",\"milk chocolate\",\"dark chocolate\"]},\"Usually yes: cocoa, milk and cocoa butter are all vegetarian. Check the bar for gelatin in chewy or marshmallow fillings, and remember whey is fine for a vegetarian but not for a vegan.\"]}]}")?;
